WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.110
I'm outside the CBS Broadcast Center right now

2
00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:06.910
because the moment we've all been waiting for is here.

3
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.950
For over a week now, our show has been on the road

4
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.530
in the Drew van, driving across the country

5
00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:15.720
from California to right here in New York.

6
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.450
And many of you spotted the van and sent us your pictures.

7
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.100
I've met some great people along the way

8
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.450
and who have reached out to us while seeing the van

9
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.430
we've met Drew Gooders.

10
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.880
I met a wonderful woman who inspired me.

11
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.640
We added businesses to our small business gift guide

12
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.460
and they went on a Barrymore tour

13
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.700
and found a snake named Drew in Albuquerque, New Mexico.

14
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.050
Guess what, it's Karyn and Noah.

15
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:49.237
(audience cheers)

16
00:00:49.237 --> 00:00:50.070
Hi Drew.

17
00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:50.903
We made it.

18
00:00:50.903 --> 00:00:53.920
Oh my gosh, finally, you guys are here.

19
00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:54.753
We are, we are.

20
00:00:54.753 --> 00:00:58.310
It's so good to see you in person, hello.

21
00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:02.380
Thank you for letting us put our logo on your van

22
00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.380
which is just so well done.

23
00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:06.438
Thank you.

24
00:01:06.438 --> 00:01:09.773
You really decked it out and created a lifestyle, really.

25
00:01:11.016 --> 00:01:12.390
It's meant to be an experience.

26
00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:13.860
It's really not meant to be a thing.

27
00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.400 line:15%
It's meant to facilitate seeing the world.

28
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.330 line:15%
And that's what this is about.

29
00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:18.320 line:15%
And also for the record

30
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.320 line:15%
you don't need a van to see the world, just go.

31
00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.550
Thank you for being the representatives

32
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:27.531
of showing people what's possible to do with their life.

33
00:01:27.531 --> 00:01:28.364
Oh, you're so welcome.

34
00:01:28.364 --> 00:01:31.520
We think that spontaneity equals joy.

35
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.210
Our lives are so regimented

36
00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:34.490
and when you can break out of that,

37
00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.980
even if it's for a long weekend

38
00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:41.350
you have the ability to just stop and be in the moment

39
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.270 line:15%
go wherever your fancy takes you.

40
00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:45.400 line:15%
I mean, it's this freedom that we just don't have.

41
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.390 line:15%
I mean, especially in this COVID year, right?

42
00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:50.680
I know, and yet people I think have been more inventive

43
00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.400
about road tripping.

44
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.070
What do you say to people that are too scared

45
00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:00.780
to let go of the permanence and comfort of their position

46
00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:05.500
or job and hop in a van and go see the world?

47
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.540
I think that's actually changed a lot in the last year.

48
00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:09.510
Living in the Bay area,

49
00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.510
we were very close to Silicon Valley.

50
00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.210
There's actually a new term that's emerged

51
00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:15.320
called the digital nomads.

52
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.270
People who actually want to work from their vehicle,

53
00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:20.080
work from their van, work from their car,

54
00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.910
Airbnb around the world and work.

55
00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.150
And I think it's a new thing.

56
00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.240
It's a new emerging thing that I think is going to catch on.

57
00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.365
A lot of companies are not going to go back to work.

58
00:02:29.365 --> 00:02:31.050
And so I think this is kind of here to stay.

59
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.610
And so in our little way, we've contributed to that.

60
00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.070
There's so many other ways that you can do that

61
00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:39.670
and that have emerged that facilitate that.

62
00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:41.780
Well, I think when people see your van

63
00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.670
and see how livable it is and stylish and beautiful

64
00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.980
it's going to be a huge source of inspiration.

65
00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.710
And I think it's confidence building what you guys do.

66
00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:50.920
Is like, "Go for it.

67
00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.320
Life is short, live your dreams.

68
00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:58.320
And make the most of the time we have here on our planet."

69
00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.160
So I am so excited about this.

70
00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.910
Now I heard there's actually a montage we get to watch

71
00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.930
of the sticker idea.

72
00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:11.310
My 90s zine girl that wants to throw Drew's News stickers.

73
00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.680
I am dying.

74
00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.720
I can't even help it or hold back.

75
00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:15.910
I just want to see it.

76
00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:19.300
It's amazing, we got to go to the best places and do that.

77
00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.133
Oh my gosh.

78
00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.860
Can I tell you where we did our favorite?

79
00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:22.693
Yes.

80
00:03:22.693 --> 00:03:25.330 line:15%
We did Cadillac Ranch in Texas.

81
00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:28.320 line:15%
Amazing art installation in the middle of the desert.

82
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.970 line:15%
We did the Twin Arrows trading post in Arizona

83
00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:34.710 line:15%
which is like these huge skyscraper sized arrows

84
00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:37.480 line:15%
that looked like they'd been shot into the desert floor.

85
00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.940 line:15%
Incredible, on Route 66.

86
00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:43.320 line:15%
We did, oh the Baghdad Cafe.

87
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.693 line:15%
Remember the movie?

88
00:03:44.693 --> 00:03:45.630 line:15%
Yes.

89
00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.240 line:15%
Amazing, it's still there.

90
00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.470 line:15%
And then we did Sun Studios in Memphis, Tennessee

91
00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:52.690 line:15%
where Elvis got his star.
Oh my gosh.

92
00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:53.890 line:15%
Elvis, Johnny Cash, yeah.

93
00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.000 line:15%
Oh my gosh.
It was amazing.

94
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.400
There are Drew's News stickers

95
00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.272
right outside Elvis' studio.

96
00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:03.022
Oh my gosh, I can't believe it!

97
00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.010
Can I ask, definitely a highlight for me

98
00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.490
watching you guys was the Drew snake.

99
00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:11.323
I don't know why.

100
00:04:11.323 --> 00:04:12.660
I just have a lot of affinity

101
00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.823
for this albino snake named Drew.

102
00:04:15.905 --> 00:04:17.450
A rattler I believe.

103
00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:18.470
Oh yeah, uh-huh.
Yeah, oh yeah.

104
00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:21.750
Was there any geographical location or landmark

105
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:25.870
or little cafe, anything that really stuck out for you

106
00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.490
as, "Gosh I wouldn't have thought that that would be

107
00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.737
such a highlight but it turned out to be?"

108
00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.650
You haven't lived until you've watched

109
00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.343
the sunset in Sedona.

110
00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.020
I'm at a lack of words

111
00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.050
for describing that.
Were you at that rock?

112
00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.000
We were right there.

113
00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.237
We were directly below what was it, Bell?

114
00:04:46.237 --> 00:04:47.070
Bell Rock.

115
00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:47.903
Bell Rock.
Oh wow.

116
00:04:47.903 --> 00:04:49.530
We climbed sort of a third of the way up Bell Rock

117
00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.110
and watched the sunset.

118
00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:52.300
We sat on top of the van

119
00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.710
which has a cool little van life shake.

120
00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:55.500
You can actually sit up on top of the van.

121
00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.540
We watched the stars for an hour and a half

122
00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.410
on the side of the road.

123
00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.730
We saw this really weird, we thought it was a UFO

124
00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:01.563
at the time.

125
00:05:01.563 --> 00:05:02.680
Turns out it was a bunch of satellites

126
00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:03.650
that launched last week

127
00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.208
that were spreading themselves across.

128
00:05:05.208 --> 00:05:06.041
So they say.

129
00:05:06.041 --> 00:05:07.160
So they say.
So they say, yeah.

130
00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:07.993
It is Sedona.

131
00:05:07.993 --> 00:05:11.740
Yeah, that isn't far from was it Area 54?

132
00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:12.573
Right down the road.
Right down 51.

133
00:05:12.573 --> 00:05:14.750
Yeah, not that far.
Exactly.

134
00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:17.210
And we just watched the stars and lay there.

135
00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.630
And honestly, one of the best things about this,

136
00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:22.550
we love, love, love our children they're amazing.

137
00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.990
It's been 14 years since Karyn and I got to go away

138
00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.893
just the two of us for more than a night here there.

139
00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.100
Thank you for that.

140
00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.830
I am so happy for you.

141
00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.330
I have to say we found it surprisingly easy to let go.

142
00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.900
I thought there was going to be more guilt.

143
00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.177
I thought there was going to be more,

144
00:05:39.177 --> 00:05:40.817
"I need to call home now."

145
00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:43.510
We were able to relax.

146
00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:46.460
I think we're going to go home a 100% recharged.

147
00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.930
This was the greatest gift in these times.

148
00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:49.763
Thank you so much.

149
00:05:49.763 --> 00:05:52.300
That makes me so happy.

150
00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.360
Oh, what a good thing to come out of this.

151
00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:56.320
But we have to go to a quick commercial break.

152
00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.270
But when we come back,

153
00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:00.950
Noah and Karyn are revealing their road tripping tips

154
00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:05.110
to make your next vacation so delightful.

155
00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:07.030
And if there's anyone, I want to hear it from

156
00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:11.003
it's two people that feel as fulfilled as you do.

157
00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:13.586 line:15%
(upbeat music)

158
00:06:15.055 --> 00:06:17.067 line:15%
